{"parameters": {}, "expected_outcome": "inventory_delta", "situation_assessment": "The shelter shell at anchor (13,112,-9) has only 4/23 blocks placed (wall_coverage=0.643, roof_coverage=0). The build_pattern failed in cycle-0015 because inventory has NO solid build materials — only stick:2, white_bed:1, wooden_pickaxe:1. The nearest oak_log is at (13,112,-8) at distance 1.56, well within reach. Mining cobblestone was blocked in cycle-0013 and build_pattern failed in cycle-0015, both in do_not_repeat. The immediate prerequisite for continuing the shelter is gathering solid build material. Collecting the nearby oak_log is the safest path: it avoids repeating the blocked mine_block action, provides a craftable resource (1 log → 4 planks), and the log is verified in the world scan at close range.", "why_this_tool": "Collect Logs (action-card-003) directly addresses the root cause of the build_pattern failure: empty inventory of build materials. The world scan confirms an oak_log at (13,112,-8) only 1.56 blocks away at the same Y level as the actor. This is a different action card from both failed recent actions (mine_block in cycle-0013, build_pattern in cycle-0015), satisfying the do_not_repeat constraint. Once logs are in inventory, the next cycle can craft planks (craft_item) and then resume build_pattern with actual materials. The direct primitive is preferred over the actor-owned action-card-020 which has readiness \"risky\".", "success_evidence": 
["inventory_delta shows oak_log count >= 1 added to inventory", "world_block_delta may show the oak_log at (13,112,-8) removed from world", "subsequent cycles can craft oak_planks from the collected log"]

, "failure_handling": "If collect_logs fails because the oak_log is unreachable or the action cannot find harvestable logs, the next turn should try mining a nearby dirt block (dirt at (14,112,-7) distance 0.75) using mine_block with blockName=\"dirt\" — this is a different parameter from the previously blocked cobblestone mine_block. If that also fails, move closer to the oak_log position and retry. Record the specific failure reason via remember to avoid blind repetition."}

